course: dictionary
lesson: 5418
title: Lactose: the sugar in milk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lactose is the natural sugar found in milk, and in foods made from milk, such as cheese, yoghurt and ice cream. Its other name is milk sugar, so when you see one of those words, you know what it means.
explain: Most people's bodies break lactose down easily. Some people's bodies cannot do this well, and we call that lactose intolerance. «Lactose intolerance means the body cannot digest milk sugar well.»
explain: The clues in the text tell you what happens next. Someone who is lactose intolerant may get tummy aches, wind or diarrhoea after drinking milk. Some people choose lactose-free milk or plant milks instead.
fact: Lactose is a sugar found naturally in milk.
fact: Cheese, yoghurt and ice cream are foods made from milk, so they contain lactose too.
fact: «Lactose intolerant» means a person's body cannot break down lactose well.
fact: An enzyme is a helper substance the body makes to break food apart.
fact: «Lactose-free milk» has the enzyme added, which breaks the lactose into simpler sugars that taste sweeter.
exercise: What is lactose? | *The natural sugar found in milk and in foods made from milk | A type of cow | A kind of salt found in bread | A brand of ice cream
exercise: «Lactose-free milk has the enzyme added.» What is an enzyme? | *A helper substance the body makes to break food apart | A type of milk | A sugar that tastes sweet
exercise: Someone who is «lactose intolerant» cannot break down lactose well. What might happen after they drink milk? | *They may get tummy aches, wind or diarrhoea | Their milk turns into lactose | They can no longer taste sweet things | They grow taller overnight
test: Why does «lactose-free milk» taste sweeter? | Cows make extra sugar in lactose-free milk | Milk is always sweeter when it is cold | The enzyme turns lactose into water | *The enzyme breaks the milk sugar into simpler sugars
test: Which of these foods is made from milk, so it contains lactose? | Rice | *Cheese | Carrots | Apples
exam: Which word means the same as «milk sugar»? | *Lactose | Enzyme | Mammal | Digest
